 is a city of profound historical and cultural significance, particularly during the Renaissance and the Enlightenment. Established in the early 13th century, it became a prominent center for intellectual and academic pursuits, notably due to the founding of Heidelberg University in 1386, which is one of the oldest universities in Germany and has been a cradle for many influential thinkers, including philosopher Georg Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel.

